1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,255
What if you texted Voyager 1 right now?

2
00:00:02,750 --> 00:00:04,727
On November eighteenth, 2026,

3
00:00:04,727 --> 00:00:09,500
it became the first spacecraft ever to reach one light-day from Earth.

4
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:12,295
About twenty-six billion kilometers away.

5
00:00:12,783 --> 00:00:17,322
Your message flies at the speed of light, and still takes a full day to arrive.

6
00:00:17,322 --> 00:00:18,930
The reply takes another day.

7
00:00:19,417 --> 00:00:20,817
It launched in 1977,

8
00:00:20,817 --> 00:00:25,367
and it's still flying at about seventeen kilometers every second.

9
00:00:25,667 --> 00:00:28,024
Like and subscribe for more space what-ifs.

10
00:00:28,517 --> 00:00:33,128
Its nuclear power drops about four watts a year, so most instruments are off.

11
00:00:33,128 --> 00:00:34,146
Two are still on.

12
00:00:34,650 --> 00:00:37,068
And right now, the team is living this.

13
00:00:37,068 --> 00:00:41,160
Since November fourteenth, Voyager has sent a signal, but no data.

14
00:00:41,160 --> 00:00:43,392
Every test takes two days to answer.

15
00:00:43,883 --> 00:00:46,182
Closer to home, we just reached Mercury.

16
00:00:46,182 --> 00:00:47,676
Full story on the channel.
